<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Caribbean Fury #4 Show of Force, 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Caribbean Fury #4 Show of Force, 1994&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;19 Feb 1994, 1800 Zulu, 1400 Local&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is the&amp;nbsp;fourth scenario of a short campaign linked to the Northern Fury series and you may wish to refer to that background &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/blog/post19/"&gt;document&lt;/A&gt; to get a broader picture of the geopolitical setting. The situation in the Caribbean is somewhat unique in that it is a small ‘side show’ to the great events occurring in Europe, the North Atlantic and Pacific. However, it is of vital interest to NATO’s largest partner – the US, and also important to the British, Dutch and French, all holding on to the vestiges of their colonial empires. The American government and military commanders want to quickly stabilize the situation here and get on with fighting the real war. There is an evolving problem however – Venezuela, and the Soviet forces being harbored there.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Cuba, Honduras and Nicaragua have now been neutralized and the Guatemalan backed insurgency in Belize has at least been contained, so the Soviets only have one major player remaining in the region. Venezuela however, is playing a dangerous game with both sides in the conflict. See the &lt;A href="http://northernfury.us/blog/post20/"&gt;Caribbean Fury background document&lt;/A&gt; for further insight on the background and specific issues in the Caribbean.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The US has no desire to drawing Venezuela into the war. So, in an effort to placate its NATO allies, eliminate Soviet capability in the region, and to show Venezuela the power and reach of the US military, a plan has been developed to use stealth to strike a stunning lance into the boil.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In this scenario you fill the role of Commander 49&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Fighter Wing US Air Force. With a combination of F-117 Strike Fighters, a B-2 Stealth Bomber and reconnaissance from an SR-71 you are to conduct a strike on Manodez Air Base in Venezuela. In addition to destroying any Soviet aircraft located there, your targets include communications and command infrastructure being used by the Soviets. You are not to be detected.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Background&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Cold War continued with no thaw in relations. Germany’s reunification has caused friction between East &amp;amp; West. WP still alive and doing very well.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Winter Olympics in Lillehammer turned into a fiasco when Soviet and eastern block teams failed to turn up for the opening ceremonies. Norway canceled the games and after some deliberation started to mobilize.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;War broke out across the globe around mid day on Sunday 13 Feb 94.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;In the Caribbean, Cuba, Honduras and Nicaragua joined the fray, somewhat haphazardly but for the first 18 hours had US and limited NATO forces off balance. However, over the past days the situation has stabilized.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Cuba, reinforced by some high end Soviet aircraft and SAM systems launched a devastating raid on Key West. Although there was some initial success, revenge was swift and a new government in Havana has called for a cease fire. Negotiations are ongoing but Cuban airspace is closed for NATO forces to allow the settlement to be finalized.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Honduras and Nicaragua have been nocked out of the war and the Guatemalan backed insurgency in Belize has been contained.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designer’s notes&lt;/STRONG&gt;:&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;UL&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You should turn 'special messages' ON.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You will get points for destroying specific infrastructure and any Soviet aircraft or units.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You loose points and risk Venezuela being drawn into the war if you are detected.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;There are plenty of older non-stealth aircraft available, you may chose to use these as a distraction or a quick reaction force but they should not venture or be detected over Venezuelan territory.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Air to Air refueling will be an issue and close planning will be required. KC-135Qs should be the only tanker to refuel the SR-71.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The SR-71 is a strategic asset, as is the B-2 bomber; loss of these assets will be a major blow to US and are penalized heavily.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;This scenario is built with angsters excellent Search and Rescue script as modified by TyphoonFR.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Created by Bart Gauvin; AKA Gunner 98&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
